     {
      "_key": "MBeO7ojrohBwl7F7zAPFEI",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I am a naturally curious person, with broad experience in zoology, ecology, and reproductive justice. I see our environment and people's wellbeing ignored by this government and I want to help change that. People deserve a representative government, not one that prioritizes profits over people. As a Kiwi-American, I also see U.S. politics and policies coming through in this government, which is a red flag and a threat to democracy."
     },
     {
      "_key": "MBeO7ojrohBwl7F7zAPFH8",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I have communicated complex topics with people in the community for decades as an educator. I earned a B.S in Zoology and a M.S. in Ecology, Evolution, and Behaviour, with a focus on monarch butterfly conservation and citizen-science research. I am a co-author of several academic papers and book chapters on monarch butterfly conservation. Additionally, I am the Co-President of Abortion Rights Aotearoa's (ALRANZ), which focuses on expanding healthcare access throughout the motu."
     },
     {
      "_key": "MBeO7ojrohBwl7F7zAPFJy",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Advocate for housing development to be removed from the Fast-track process."
     },
     {
      "_key": "MBeO7ojrohBwl7F7zAPFMo",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Prioritise funding for public healthcare services so it is equitable and accessible for everyone."
     },
     {
      "_key": "MBeO7ojrohBwl7F7zAPFPe",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Restore Equal Pay agreements, removed by this government, and pay professionals what they are due."
     }
    ],
